{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-composite-crossing-parity","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:composite-crossing-parity","kind":"proposition","title":"Sublimation from shell-filling representation theory","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-borromean-quark","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-shell-structure-eigenvalues","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-noble-gas-characterization"],"tags":["sublimation","shell-structure","young-diagram","hecke-representation","phase-transition","magic-numbers"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.crossing_parity_eq_Z","text":"composite-crossing-parity.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/composite-crossing-parity.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:composite-crossing-parity\"></a><p><strong>Proposition (conditional on <a href=\"#conj:borromean-quark\">conj:borromean-quark</a>).</strong> Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}(Z, N)</code> be a stable atom with electron configuration occupying shells <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_1, \\ldots, S_k</code>. The complete decomposition</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  V^{\\otimes n} \\cong \\bigoplus_{\\lambda \\vdash n,\\, \\ell(\\lambda) \\leq 2} V_\\lambda \\otimes S_\\lambda</code></pre>\n<p>simultaneously determines the nuclear shell structure and the thermodynamic phase behavior through the identical Hecke algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(q)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/composite-crossing-parity.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"21.10.2"}
